            if str1[i - 1] == str2[j - 1]:
                dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1
            else:
                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])

    if m == n:
        return dp[m][n]
    else:
        return max(dp[m][n], dp[m - 1][n - 1])
```
This version of the function checks if the input strings have the same length, and if not, it returns the maximum of the longest common subsequence length and the length of the shorter string. This approach ensures that the function can handle variations in input string lengths gracefully. It is designed to check for length equality, and if the lengths are not equal, it ensures that the function still operates correctly by returning the maximum of the calculated longest common subsequence length and the length of the shorter string. By doing so, the function maintains its utility and correctness across different input scenarios, ensuring that it remains robust and reliable.
